WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.890
You may not heard of this
mention many acronyms for

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.960
Native Apps monetization but
they do exist.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.130
Let's take a look at a few of them.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.900
First, we talked about
in-app purchases a bit.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.680
You may see this abbreviated as IAP.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:20.680
Important metrics to measure,
especially with IAP are ARPU and ARPPU.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.380
ARPU, or average revenue per user,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.780
is calculated by dividing your total
revenue by your total number of users.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:35.550
ARPPU, or average revenue per
paying user, is calculated by

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:40.390
dividing the total revenue by the total
number of users that made a purchase.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.920
The advertising terms we discussed back
in the website monetization section

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.410
also apply here.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.620
So if you wanted to implement ads in you
native app, we recommend you go back and

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.490
check out that content.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.910
Now it's once again time to test
your memory skills with another

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.430
acronym challenge.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.390
See if you can recall
the definitions for

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.980
each of these terms
that we just discussed.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.780
Enter their meanings
in the boxes provided.

